WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.276
Take a step back and look at what's in this orrery.

00:00:04.276 --> 00:00:09.558
Apollo 11 — Neil Armstrong's first footstep — happened in 1969.

00:00:09.558 --> 00:00:13.163
Voyager left for the outer planets in 1977.

00:00:13.163 --> 00:00:15.510
Hubble began seeing in 1990.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:19.702
Sojourner became the first wheels on Mars in 1997.

00:00:19.702 --> 00:00:24.984
Lunokhod had wheels on the Moon twenty-seven years before that.

00:00:24.984 --> 00:00:32.194
Chang'e 4 landed on the far side of the Moon in 2019 — the first lander ever to do so.

00:00:32.194 --> 00:00:37.225
Chandrayaan-3 placed wheels at the lunar south pole in 2023.

00:00:37.225 --> 00:00:39.153
Read those names again.

00:00:39.153 --> 00:00:39.572
NASA.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:39.907
ESA.

00:00:39.907 --> 00:00:40.746
Roscosmos.

00:00:40.746 --> 00:00:41.165
CNSA.

00:00:41.165 --> 00:00:41.584
ISRO.

00:00:41.584 --> 00:00:42.003
JAXA.

00:00:42.003 --> 00:00:42.339
CSA.

00:00:42.339 --> 00:00:43.009
SpaceIL.

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.267
Eight agencies.

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:45.608
Five continents.

00:00:45.608 --> 00:00:48.543
No single nation built this orrery.

00:00:48.543 --> 00:00:50.303
No single decade did.

00:00:50.303 --> 00:01:11.431
What you're looking at is the result of cooperative competition across seventy years — countries that disagree about almost everything on Earth agreeing, by their actions, to do the same hard thing in slightly different ways, and then sharing the data.

00:01:11.431 --> 00:01:14.281
Apollo was the first time we left.

00:01:14.281 --> 00:01:17.803
Artemis is the first time we plan to stay.

00:01:17.803 --> 00:01:27.779
A crewed Mars mission will be the first time we go to a place from which a same-week return is not physically possible.

00:01:27.779 --> 00:01:31.217
Each step on this ladder taught the next.

00:01:31.217 --> 00:01:34.990
Each agency on this ladder taught the others.

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:39.936
The orrery in front of you is not a map of accomplishments.

00:01:39.936 --> 00:01:46.224
It is a map of what we now know is possible — because somebody has done it.

